{
  "case_id": "2012-12-52",
  "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nANDRE D. BOUFFARD, ESQ., Burlington, Vermont; on behalf of Petitioner.\nBRIAN C. SHAUGHNESSY, ESQ., Manchester, New Hampshire; on behalf of Respondent.\nLEWIS S. YELIN, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue in this case is whether Section 14501 of the United States Transportation Code expressly preempts the Respondent's State law consumer protection in tort claims for damages against a tow trucker who towed his vehicle lawfully and then, several months later, disposed of the vehicle after the fees for towing and storage had not been paid."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Both of these claims are preempted because they are directed at the conduct -- the type of conduct that tow truck companies all over this country every day engage in, in dealing with a particular type of tow that's referred to in the business as nonconsensual tows."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "law that applies only to the towing companies who tow the automobile and then store it, or does the law apply, say, to a garage, say, someone brings a car to a garage for repairs, and does this storage law regulate garage operations as well as towing operations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And are all those things preempted? I would be amazed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It -- it includes storage, is the point you are coming to, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, there's a lot of language in the majority pretty much along the line that Justice Scalia said. And not sure if that\u2019s your point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: That's your problem, which is, what is it directed to? And that's the real"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bouffard",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOUFFARD: Well, Justice Breyer, let me just say, first of all, that -- that consumer protection is -- is -- I'm not sure I would concede that consumer protection is -- is an area of traditional State regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Suppose, Mr. Shaughnessy, that the New Hampshire laws were more onerous than they are. Suppose they said to a towing company, once you've towed this car you have to hold on to it forever. Or suppose they said to the towing company, you have to hire private investigators to go figure out who owns this car. Would any of those be preempted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "\"Moreover, criminal laws prohibiting theft are not the kind of burdensome State economic regulation Congress sought to prevent with the FAAAA, nor are abandoned vehicle laws such as New Hampshire Chapter 262 in its regulations which do not hamper the operations of tow truckers. Instead they establish procedures for the efficient handling and disposition of abandoned vehicles.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YELIN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Congress deregulated the trucking industry Alderson Reporting Company"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to eliminate undue interference with market forces and consumer choice. But market forces and consumer choice cannot operate on the sale of nonconsensually towed cars, and there's little reason to think that Congress intended to preempt State laws that regulate that conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I don't understand what you just said. Say it again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: So it would depend upon how severe the consumer protection law is, is that right? If it's a consumer protection law that really whacks the tow truck operator, that would be different from a moderate, benign consumer protection law? We have to examine each consumer protection law on its own, is that it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-12-52",
      "confidence": 0.0,
